        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lynyrd Skynyrd band members, backup singer\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd, L&J Company\n- Events: 1977 Convair CV-240 crash\n- Places: Addison, Texas, Gillsburg, Mississippi, Greenville, South Carolina, Baton Rouge, Louisiana\n- Products: Gimme Back My Bullets\n\nFacts:\n- Gimme Back My Bullets is Lynyrd Skynyrd's fourth studio album.\n- On October 20, 1977, a Convair CV-240 chartered by Lynyrd Skynyrd from L&J Company of Addison, Texas, ran out of fuel and crashed in Gillsburg, Mississippi, near the end of a flight from Greenville, South Carolina, to Baton Rouge, Louisiana.\n- In 1977, two Lynyrd Skynyrd band members and a backup singer died in the airplane crash, ending the band's most popular incarnation at the peak of its success.",
